title: Add storage invariant checks to pallet-psm try_state

doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      This PR adds `do_try_state` to `pallet-psm`. The `try_state` hook calls it
      with the `try-runtime` feature. Seventeen checks cover the storage layout of
      the multi-instance PSM. They confirm that each decimals snapshot agrees with
      the live asset metadata, that each reserve covers the debt against it, that
      the issuance of the internal asset covers the debt of the instance, that no
      row stays after the removal of its PSM, and that no debt exists for a pair
      that the PSM does not approve.

      Four checks are advisory. An advisory check writes a warning to the log, and
      it does not return an error. Governance can create these four states
      correctly: debt above a per-asset ceiling, debt above the ceiling of an
      instance, a reserve with a balance but with zero weight and zero debt, and a
      fee row for an external asset that the PSM does not yet approve.

      Each check has a unit test. A test changes one storage item, then it confirms
      the specific error. A test of an advisory check confirms the result is `Ok`.

crates:
  - name: pallet-psm
    bump: minor
